1
00:02:30,059 --> 00:02:35,059
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,059 --> 00:02:40,059
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,059 --> 00:02:44,059
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,059 --> 00:02:49,059
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,059 --> 00:02:52,059
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,059 --> 00:02:55,059
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:55,059 --> 00:02:58,059
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:58,059 --> 00:03:01,059
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:01,059 --> 00:03:04,059
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:04,059 --> 00:03:07,059
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,059 --> 00:03:11,059
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,059 --> 00:03:15,059
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:18,059 --> 00:03:23,059
After the War of the Best in Marineford, Luffy was transported to the Maiden Island,

14
00:03:23,059 --> 00:03:26,059
where grief over the loss of Ace consumed him.

15
00:03:26,059 --> 00:03:31,059
You still have something left in this world to treasure, don't you?

16
00:03:37,059 --> 00:03:41,059
Reunited with Dark King Rayleigh, decision time for Luffy!

17
00:03:56,059 --> 00:04:01,059
Oh, listen, I think the kid stopped screaming.

18
00:04:01,059 --> 00:04:02,059
Yeah, about that.

19
00:04:02,059 --> 00:04:05,059
Where did Straw Hat run off to anyway?

20
00:04:05,059 --> 00:04:08,059
I mean, he's gonna die if that wound opens up, right?

21
00:04:11,059 --> 00:04:12,059
Huh?

22
00:04:12,059 --> 00:04:13,059
Ah!

23
00:04:13,059 --> 00:04:15,059
I got one! Nice!

24
00:04:18,059 --> 00:04:19,059
Huh?

25
00:04:19,059 --> 00:04:23,059
Hey, what the hell?

26
00:04:23,059 --> 00:04:26,059
I think I saw something moving.

27
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:28,059
Whoa!

28
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:29,059
It's huge!

29
00:04:40,059 --> 00:04:41,059
Damn!

30
00:04:41,059 --> 00:04:42,059
That is the biggest sea king I've ever seen!

31
00:04:42,059 --> 00:04:43,059
Why is it flipping out?

32
00:04:43,059 --> 00:04:44,059
It's scary!

33
00:04:53,059 --> 00:04:54,059
It's dead!

34
00:04:54,059 --> 00:04:55,059
Something killed it!

35
00:04:56,059 --> 00:04:57,059
You gotta be joking!

36
00:04:57,059 --> 00:04:59,059
I didn't get a look at what happened!

37
00:04:59,059 --> 00:05:01,059
I don't think I like this place!

38
00:05:01,059 --> 00:05:02,059
Whoa!

39
00:05:02,059 --> 00:05:03,059
Is that a man?

40
00:05:03,059 --> 00:05:04,059
Hey!

41
00:05:04,059 --> 00:05:05,059
Who are you?

42
00:05:05,059 --> 00:05:06,059
What a doozy!

43
00:05:06,059 --> 00:05:07,059
Whoa!

44
00:05:07,059 --> 00:05:08,059
It's you!

45
00:05:08,059 --> 00:05:09,059
The Dark King Silver's Rayleigh!

46
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:10,059
What?

47
00:05:10,059 --> 00:05:11,059
Oh, it's been a while.

48
00:05:11,059 --> 00:05:13,059
I remember meeting you at Saba Odie.

49
00:05:15,059 --> 00:05:18,059
It's Gold Rogers' first mate right here in the flesh!

50
00:05:18,059 --> 00:05:19,059
So, funny story.

51
00:05:19,059 --> 00:05:20,059
Things got kind of rocky in the storm.

52
00:05:20,059 --> 00:05:23,059
My ship sank so I had no choice but to swim in.

53
00:05:23,059 --> 00:05:24,059
The End of the War.

54
00:05:24,059 --> 00:05:25,059
The End of the War.

55
00:05:25,059 --> 00:05:26,059
Oh, what a doozy.

56
00:05:26,059 --> 00:05:27,059
It's you!

57
00:05:27,059 --> 00:05:28,059
The Dark King Silver's Rayleigh!

58
00:05:28,059 --> 00:05:29,059
What?

59
00:05:29,059 --> 00:05:30,059
It's you!

60
00:05:30,059 --> 00:05:31,059
The Dark King Silver's Rayleigh!

61
00:05:31,059 --> 00:05:32,059
What?

62
00:05:32,059 --> 00:05:33,059
Oh, it's been a while.

63
00:05:33,059 --> 00:05:34,059
I remember meeting you at Saba Odie.

64
00:05:34,059 --> 00:05:35,059
It's Gold Rogers' first mate right here in the flesh!

65
00:05:35,059 --> 00:05:36,059
So, funny story.

66
00:05:36,059 --> 00:05:39,059
Things got kind of rocky in the storm.

67
00:05:39,059 --> 00:05:41,059
so I had no choice but to swim here.

68
00:05:41,059 --> 00:05:42,059
What?

69
00:05:42,059 --> 00:05:44,059
But they never have storms in this part of the sea.

70
00:05:44,059 --> 00:05:46,059
That's why they call it the Calm Belt.

71
00:05:46,059 --> 00:05:47,059
But then that must mean...

72
00:05:47,059 --> 00:05:51,059
He crashed in safe waters and swam through that bed of sea kings?

73
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:53,059
How is that supposed to work?

74
00:05:53,059 --> 00:05:55,059
I have a pretty good breaststroke.

75
00:05:55,059 --> 00:05:57,059
Right. He says it like it's no big deal.

76
00:05:57,059 --> 00:06:00,059
So you killed that giant thing...

77
00:06:00,059 --> 00:06:02,059
with your bare hands?

78
00:06:02,059 --> 00:06:05,059
I have actual bare hands and I couldn't do that.

79
00:06:07,059 --> 00:06:09,059
Forgive me, Dark King.

80
00:06:09,059 --> 00:06:11,059
What are you even sorry for?

81
00:06:11,059 --> 00:06:13,059
Let me be frank.

82
00:06:15,059 --> 00:06:17,059
Something tells me Luffy's on this island.

83
00:06:17,059 --> 00:06:19,059
Is that correct?

84
00:06:23,059 --> 00:06:24,059
Have you heard the news?

85
00:06:24,059 --> 00:06:27,059
The princess and some others just left to deliver food to Luffy.

86
00:06:27,059 --> 00:06:29,059
They're so lucky.

87
00:06:29,059 --> 00:06:32,059
I want to make those cheeks of his stretch and stretch and stretch.

88
00:06:32,059 --> 00:06:34,059
I heard they'll invite him over once all his wounds heal.

89
00:06:34,059 --> 00:06:36,059
It should be any day now.

90
00:06:36,059 --> 00:06:37,059
We should hold a feast again.

91
00:06:37,059 --> 00:06:41,059
It's a shame he's hurt, but I'm glad he came back so soon.

92
00:06:41,059 --> 00:06:44,059
Men sure are fascinating creatures, aren't they?

93
00:06:44,059 --> 00:06:49,059
I wish I could be one just for a little while so I could have fun and be stretchy too.

94
00:06:49,059 --> 00:06:51,059
He shall stretch enough for all of us!

95
00:06:51,059 --> 00:06:55,059
Well, since he's here again, maybe I'll make him another pair of clothes.

96
00:06:55,059 --> 00:06:57,059
Without all the frills.

97
00:06:57,059 --> 00:07:07,059
How shameful it is for newlyweds to be separated like this. What a tragic heroine I've become.

98
00:07:07,059 --> 00:07:13,059
Sweetie, don't say that. You know, we're always together in spirit.

99
00:07:13,059 --> 00:07:14,059
Of course, dear.

100
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:19,059
No matter how far apart the world may keep us, we are bound by a thread of passion.

101
00:07:19,059 --> 00:07:27,059
Oh, Luffy. You always know just what to say. My heart is aflame with affection. I can feel the desire building up inside me.

102
00:07:27,059 --> 00:07:35,059
You are hopeless! How foolish! I've told you, any man may remember your name, but that doesn't mean that you're married!

103
00:07:35,059 --> 00:07:39,059
Oh? Then what is marriage? What else is there to do?

104
00:07:39,059 --> 00:07:42,059
That is a difficult question to answer.

105
00:07:45,059 --> 00:07:48,059
You're too weak to travel to Saba Ori, especially with that wound.

106
00:07:48,059 --> 00:07:55,059
I'll make it work. I gotta see my friends as soon as possible. They'll be expecting me. I promised them I'd be there.

107
00:07:55,059 --> 00:07:57,059
Well, nevertheless.

108
00:07:59,059 --> 00:08:03,059
Now that's odd. The submarine is gone. Surely they didn't depart.

109
00:08:03,059 --> 00:08:05,059
Oh, hello there, Luffy.

110
00:08:05,059 --> 00:08:08,059
Huh? It's Rayleigh, the old guy.

111
00:08:09,059 --> 00:08:11,059
Straightforward as ever, I see.

112
00:08:11,059 --> 00:08:18,059
Why are you here? I was about to use my Viva card to go to Saba Ori, since my friend should be waiting there.

113
00:08:19,059 --> 00:08:21,059
So, did you see them?

114
00:08:21,059 --> 00:08:24,059
I haven't. Actually, it seems they haven't made it there yet.

115
00:08:24,059 --> 00:08:29,059
As for my Viva card, I ended up handing it off to Shaki. It's rather nice.

116
00:08:29,059 --> 00:08:33,059
No one can find me, and I can go wherever I please.

117
00:08:33,059 --> 00:08:38,059
Dark King Rayleigh, I don't believe this. Is it really you?

118
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:40,059
Hm. You must be that former warlord.

119
00:08:41,059 --> 00:08:44,059
Yeah, that's right. You saved my life at Marineford.

120
00:08:44,059 --> 00:08:45,059
Hm?

121
00:08:46,059 --> 00:08:47,059
Something wrong?

122
00:08:47,059 --> 00:08:51,059
I didn't expect to come face to face with a living legend.

123
00:08:51,059 --> 00:08:54,059
Huh. I suppose you'd like your hat back.

124
00:08:54,059 --> 00:08:56,059
Oh, yeah. Thanks.

125
00:09:00,059 --> 00:09:04,059
My head just doesn't feel right without it. There, that's a lot better.

126
00:09:04,059 --> 00:09:06,059
Hm.

127
00:09:07,059 --> 00:09:10,059
Have you seen a group of pirates or a submarine around here?

128
00:09:10,059 --> 00:09:13,059
If you're talking about Trafalgar Law, he took off.

129
00:09:14,059 --> 00:09:16,059
He left a message for Luffy.

130
00:09:17,059 --> 00:09:19,059
Stay in bed for two more weeks.

131
00:09:21,059 --> 00:09:23,059
He saved your life, didn't he?

132
00:09:29,059 --> 00:09:32,059
Now that was a raw deal. All those women right there.

133
00:09:32,059 --> 00:09:35,059
And we were stuck on the shore. Man, what a tease.

134
00:09:35,059 --> 00:09:37,059
They said bears were welcome to visit, though.

135
00:09:37,059 --> 00:09:39,059
Hey, don't tell us that!

136
00:09:40,059 --> 00:09:41,059
I'm sorry.

137
00:09:41,059 --> 00:09:42,059
Who cares?

138
00:09:43,059 --> 00:09:45,059
I wonder what the Dark King is up to.

139
00:09:45,059 --> 00:09:48,059
Seems he's drawn to another man with the will of Dee.

140
00:09:48,059 --> 00:09:49,059
Hm.

141
00:09:49,059 --> 00:09:52,059
Well, whatever happens, it's bound to be a storm.

142
00:09:53,059 --> 00:09:57,059
No! It can't be! Rayleigh, is that really you?

143
00:09:57,059 --> 00:09:59,059
Oh, why hello, Gloriosa.

144
00:10:00,059 --> 00:10:01,059
It sure has been a while.

145
00:10:01,059 --> 00:10:03,059
Hi, Rayleigh. How are you?

146
00:10:04,059 --> 00:10:06,059
I'm lovely. Good to see you.

147
00:10:06,059 --> 00:10:07,059
It's Luffy!

148
00:10:07,059 --> 00:10:09,059
Could you show some manners for once?

149
00:10:09,059 --> 00:10:11,059
Don't ignore the man who saved your life.

150
00:10:12,059 --> 00:10:15,059
He saved your life so the three of you know old man Rayleigh too?

151
00:10:15,059 --> 00:10:16,059
Indeed.

152
00:10:17,059 --> 00:10:19,059
It's a long story. We'll spare you the details.

153
00:10:19,059 --> 00:10:21,059
I'm so glad to see that you're well.

154
00:10:21,059 --> 00:10:23,059
I've been awake for days worrying about you.

155
00:10:24,059 --> 00:10:25,059
You must be starving.

156
00:10:25,059 --> 00:10:28,059
I've brought plenty of food. Please eat to your heart's content.

157
00:10:29,059 --> 00:10:31,059
You can't even bear to look at him.

158
00:10:31,059 --> 00:10:34,059
How is this marriage of yours supposed to work out?

159
00:10:34,059 --> 00:10:35,059
Serve the man!

160
00:10:36,059 --> 00:10:38,059
Give him some food and be quick about it!

161
00:10:42,059 --> 00:10:43,059
No, Jinbei!

162
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:46,059
This cornucopia was not meant for you!

163
00:10:46,059 --> 00:10:48,059
You may have one bite.

164
00:10:48,059 --> 00:10:49,059
How generous.

165
00:10:49,059 --> 00:10:52,059
I shall endeavor to curb my appetite.

166
00:10:55,059 --> 00:10:56,059
Come, Luffy.

167
00:10:56,059 --> 00:10:57,059
You need your strength.

168
00:10:57,059 --> 00:10:58,059
And as they say,

169
00:10:58,059 --> 00:10:59,059
to eat is to live.

170
00:10:59,059 --> 00:11:00,059
Well done.

171
00:11:16,059 --> 00:11:18,059
Back to the old Luffy already.

172
00:11:20,059 --> 00:11:21,059
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

173
00:11:22,059 --> 00:11:23,059
No!

174
00:11:24,059 --> 00:11:25,059
Ha!

175
00:11:26,059 --> 00:11:27,059
Ha!

176
00:11:27,059 --> 00:11:28,059
Ha!

177
00:11:32,059 --> 00:11:33,059
I said a bite!

178
00:11:33,059 --> 00:11:36,059
Keep stuffing your face like that and you'll leave poor Luffy with nothing!

179
00:11:40,059 --> 00:11:41,059
Hm?

180
00:11:42,059 --> 00:11:43,059
A letter from Shaki.

181
00:11:43,059 --> 00:11:45,059
Thank you for bringing this, Rayleigh.

182
00:11:46,059 --> 00:11:47,059
She hasn't changed.

183
00:11:48,059 --> 00:11:49,059
Not one bit.

184
00:11:50,059 --> 00:11:51,059
Yeah.

185
00:11:51,059 --> 00:11:52,059
If you were living in Sabaody again,

186
00:11:52,059 --> 00:11:53,059
it'd be just like old times.

187
00:11:54,059 --> 00:11:55,059
She's doing well.

188
00:11:55,059 --> 00:11:56,059
And you girls.

189
00:11:56,059 --> 00:11:59,059
You three have gotten tough over the past 13 years,

190
00:11:59,059 --> 00:12:02,059
possessing a strength that is only matched by your beauty.

191
00:12:03,059 --> 00:12:05,059
Rayleigh, Granny Nyon, and Shaki.

192
00:12:06,059 --> 00:12:10,059
If it weren't for you three, we'd still be slaves to the Celestial Dragons right now.

193
00:12:11,059 --> 00:12:12,059
This troubles me.

194
00:12:12,059 --> 00:12:17,059
If you found him, protecting Luffy may be more difficult than we thought.

195
00:12:18,059 --> 00:12:25,059
I know you're friends, but if you could find Luffy so quickly, I fear the Navy's search for him may prove successful as well.

196
00:12:26,059 --> 00:12:27,059
Then we'd all be in danger.

197
00:12:28,059 --> 00:12:29,059
Oh.

198
00:12:29,059 --> 00:12:30,059
If it isn't Rayleigh.

199
00:12:31,059 --> 00:12:32,059
It's me, Hancock.

200
00:12:32,059 --> 00:12:33,059
Do you remember me?

201
00:12:33,059 --> 00:12:34,059
Really?

202
00:12:34,059 --> 00:12:36,059
You just now noticed him?

203
00:12:37,059 --> 00:12:38,059
Don't worry.

204
00:12:38,059 --> 00:12:41,059
I doubt the Navy will guess that Luffy's staying here.

205
00:12:42,059 --> 00:12:48,059
First off, the one who helped him escape from the Sabaody Archipelago told me he sent him off in this direction.

206
00:12:51,059 --> 00:12:52,059
Huh?

207
00:12:52,059 --> 00:12:53,059
Kuma?

208
00:12:53,059 --> 00:13:01,059
I work for the Revolutionary Army. Because Straw Hat shares a connection with Dragon, I will let his crew escape.

209
00:13:02,059 --> 00:13:04,059
Oh, that's quite the twist.

210
00:13:05,059 --> 00:13:08,059
So, where did he end up sending our monkey boy?

211
00:13:09,059 --> 00:13:10,059
Beats me.

212
00:13:13,059 --> 00:13:16,059
I apologize for my abrupt manner earlier.

213
00:13:17,059 --> 00:13:19,059
Can I speak with you for a moment?

214
00:13:20,059 --> 00:13:22,059
I don't have much time.

215
00:13:23,059 --> 00:13:24,059
Not as myself.

216
00:13:26,059 --> 00:13:27,059
Now, as for Straw Hat.

217
00:13:29,059 --> 00:13:32,059
Kuma would only tell me what direction he sent our friend Luffy flying in.

218
00:13:33,059 --> 00:13:36,059
But even that info didn't necessarily point to this island.

219
00:13:37,059 --> 00:13:42,059
However, some interesting details came to light when I was looking into the events leading up to Marineford.

220
00:13:43,059 --> 00:13:47,059
Namely, the Impel Down prison break caused by Luffy and the others.

221
00:13:47,059 --> 00:13:53,059
I spent a lot of time puzzling over how Luffy was able to infiltrate such a heavily guarded prison.

222
00:13:54,059 --> 00:13:57,059
It made enough sense that Luffy got there by stowing away on a Navy ship with Hancock.

223
00:13:57,059 --> 00:13:58,059
But it still didn't add up.

224
00:13:58,059 --> 00:13:59,059
Hmm.

225
00:13:59,059 --> 00:14:07,059
Hancock is known to hate both the world government and men.

226
00:14:07,059 --> 00:14:10,059
I don't think she'd willingly get on a government ship.

227
00:14:11,059 --> 00:14:12,059
Certainly not to help a man.

228
00:14:13,059 --> 00:14:16,059
Knowing that, how else would Luffy have gotten there?

229
00:14:16,059 --> 00:14:18,059
Have you considered this one?

230
00:14:20,059 --> 00:14:24,059
Maybe Hancock met Monkey and had a case of love at first sight.

231
00:14:25,059 --> 00:14:26,059
If so, everything fits.

232
00:14:29,059 --> 00:14:31,059
He is pretty cute, after all.

233
00:14:31,059 --> 00:14:35,059
It's also a lovely way to spite the Navy.

234
00:14:36,059 --> 00:14:40,059
And now she's got the perfect opportunity to nurse her poor, injured lover boy back to hell.

235
00:14:41,059 --> 00:14:45,059
I think you're letting your imagination get carried away, Shaki.

236
00:14:48,059 --> 00:14:50,059
Guess that's the power of women's intuition.

237
00:14:51,059 --> 00:14:52,059
That's my Shaki.

238
00:14:53,059 --> 00:14:54,059
The snake princesses.

239
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:56,059
Well, see for yourself.

240
00:14:56,059 --> 00:14:57,059
Do you like it?

241
00:14:57,059 --> 00:14:58,059
Please say yes.

242
00:14:58,059 --> 00:14:59,059
It's all just for you.

243
00:14:59,059 --> 00:15:04,059
Although our little theory turned out to be true, it's still pretty ridiculous.

244
00:15:05,059 --> 00:15:07,059
So the Navy won't act on it.

245
00:15:08,059 --> 00:15:10,059
All right. It's time we got down to business.

246
00:15:12,059 --> 00:15:13,059
Hey, Luffy.

247
00:15:14,059 --> 00:15:17,059
Earlier you said you're heading back to Saboori to meet up with your crew.

248
00:15:18,059 --> 00:15:19,059
Do you still plan on doing that?

249
00:15:22,059 --> 00:15:24,059
Of course I do. They need me.

250
00:15:26,059 --> 00:15:27,059
Maybe they do.

251
00:15:27,059 --> 00:15:28,059
But is that the best choice?

252
00:15:28,059 --> 00:15:29,059
Maybe they do.

253
00:15:29,059 --> 00:15:30,059
But is that the best choice?

254
00:15:30,059 --> 00:15:31,059
Think back.

255
00:15:31,059 --> 00:15:38,059
Surely you remember how your last trip to Saboori ended.

256
00:15:38,059 --> 00:15:49,079
Think back.

257
00:15:51,579 --> 00:15:54,899
Surely you remember how your last trip to Sabahodi ended.

258
00:16:02,699 --> 00:16:03,419
Everyone!

259
00:16:04,059 --> 00:16:06,299
Start running and look after yourselves!

260
00:16:06,299 --> 00:16:08,299
We can't win this one!

